      "text": [
        " رِوَايَةِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ مُسْلِمٍ عَنْ أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ قَالَ: \"لاَ تُنْكَحُ اِبْنَةُ اَلْأَخِ وَ لاَ اِبْنَةُ اَلْأُخْتِ عَلَى عَمَّتِهَا وَ لاَ عَلَى خَالَتِهَا إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِهِمَا وَ تُنْكَحُ اَلْعَمَّةُ وَ اَلْخَالَةُ عَلَى اِبْنَةِ اَلْأَخِ وَ اِبْنَةِ اَلْأُخْتِ بِغَيْرِ إِذْنِهِمَا \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4438 - And in a narration from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Abu Ja'far Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), who said:\n\"The daughter of a brother and the daughter of a sister cannot be married alongside their paternal or maternal aunt except with their permission. However, the paternal and maternal aunt can be married alongside the daughter of a brother or the daughter of a sister without requiring their permission.\""
        ]
      }
